title: Stack overflow diagnostic instead of silent SIGSEGV (P0-6)
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: medium
blocked_by: []
created_at: '2026-06-10T03:27:51'
updated_at: '2026-06-10T03:47:06'
result: 'P0-6 verified fixed: runtime/signals.c installs SIGSEGV/SIGBUS handler distinguishing
  coroutine guard-page hits vs native-thread overflow; deep recursion prints ''jinn
  runtime: stack overflow (native thread)'' + remediation, exits 134. Already pinned
  by alpha_audit_native_stack_overflow_diagnostic.'
description: 'Stack overflow from infinite recursion produces a silent SIGSEGV with
  no output instead of a diagnostic. Fix: in `runtime/sched.c` startup, install a
  `sigaction(SIGSEGV)` handler that checks `siginfo->si_addr` against the current
  coroutine''s guard region. If inside the guard region: print "coroutine stack overflow
  at FILE:LINE (stack size 64KB; consider increasing JINN_STACK_SIZE or refactoring
  recursion)", restore default SIGSEGV, re-raise. Also review/probes2/p40_inf_recur.jn
  must produce the diagnostic. (review/14_findings.md P0-6, review/15_roadmap.md A.6)'
